pra: 0167 - recovery escalation: line reset, full controller reset, card idle+reinit

DRAFT (not committed; produced by the eMMC speed-work agent). STACKS ON
0003. Generated against the reconstructed CI-built tree (pristine
xnu-8796.141.3 + 0001..0165 with pre-skips 0031/0041/0097/0099/0127/0129,
GNU patch -p1 --fuzz=0, index lines stripped). Verify with GNU
`patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --dry-run`, NOT git apply.

PROBLEM: pra_emmc_recover() is one level - CMD12 stop + CMD|DAT soft reset
+ ready wait - and 0164's ring has never shown what happens when that is
not enough. The 0162 wedge signature (card streaming forever, DAT held)
survives a controller-side reset by definition; the driver had no second
or third move, so the boot died and took the evidence with it.

CHANGES - pra_emmc_recover() escalates, each level printed:

(a) CMD12 stop + CMD|DAT soft reset + ready wait, the 0164 recovery.
    Outcome printed rate-limited (1/10 s, running recover count): lines
    "released" or "STILL BUSY". Safe: only command/data aborts, card state
    untouched.

(b) FULL software reset - SOFTWARE_RESET = 0x7 (DAT line + CMD line + ALL)
    - then pra_emmc_ensure_clock() (the reset stops the SD clock) and a
    100k-nop settle, then ready wait. Resets ONLY the host controller:
    FIFOs, DMA state, clock engine. The card keeps its state machine, RCA
    and negotiated data path, so per-sector CMD17 - the boot's lifeline -
    works the moment the lines free; that is what makes (b) safe for the
    command path. The pre-reset HOST_CONTROL value is read and written
    back because this Arasan's reset behaviour is unverified (the spec
    says config registers survive a reset-all; belt and suspenders).
    Outcome printed.

(c) idle the CARD: CMD0, bounded CMD1 SEND_OP_COND polling (20 tries, OCR
    arg 0x40ff8080), then FULL identification: CMD2 (CID ignored), CMD3
    (assign RCA 1), CMD7 (select), CMD13 verify state==tran, then the
    boot's data path re-asserted (CMD6 BUS_WIDTH=8bit, CMD6 HS_TIMING=1,
    host control 8-bit|HS) and PROVEN with one real CMD17 read of the
    root partition's first LBA. Full identification is mandatory, not
    optional polish: CMD17 is illegal outside stby/tran/data, so a bare
    CMD0+CMD1 would leave the lifeline dead. Card-side resets revert the
    volatile EXT_CSD fields (bus width, HS timing), hence the CMD6s.
    (c) runs only after (a) AND (b) failed - per-sector reads are already
    dead - so it cannot make a working boot worse; if it fails too, the
    next exit is a power cycle, same as before this patch.

STATED UNKNOWNs (checked, not guessed):
- The boot's OCR argument was never recorded: LK initialised the card
  before this driver mapped the host and the probe prints (host/caps/
  extcsd - ring22:3-6) carry no OCR. CMD1 uses the standard
  sector-addressed pattern 0x40ff8080 (HCS=1, both voltage windows) and
  the response is printed verbatim. The R1 error mask is NOT applied to
  CMD1 (OCR busy/HCS bits would trip it).
- The boot's RCA is equally unrecorded; a fresh RCA 1 is assigned and
  printed.
- The command encodings for CMD0/1/2/3/7/13 mirror the closest existing
  command of the same class (0x1A = the proven R1 no-data family,
  0x1B = the CMD6 R1b family, 0x0000 = all-zero). None has run on this
  hardware; every step is bounded (2e5-iteration polls) and printed, and
  a mid-sequence failure ends (c) with its print.

RECOVER MOVED: pra_emmc_recover() + helpers now live after pra_emmc_tune()
so (c) can use pra_emmc_switch()/pra_emmc_read_sector(); the only caller
(strat) is defined later, so no forward declarations. The 0003-era rate-
limited outcome print of level (a) is preserved verbatim in behaviour.

DEFAULT BOOT: unchanged - recover() still runs only after a failed chunk
(2-strike latch caps it at two runs per boot) or, with 0002, after a DMA
failure (one-strike latch). Levels (b)/(c) exist behind (a)'s failure.

